; THE NORTHERN WILDS (the 2026-08-28 layout rebuild) — the frontier between the Crossway gate and the arena, and
; the cell the EncounterDirector uses more than any other.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THIS REPLACED. One 5 m path from the Crossway seam at (0, 25) south to a ruin at (0, -6),
; and then nothing: a corridor with a dead end, four dead pines, two rock clusters and four pickups
; sitting in the open beside the path. Everything the cell had was on the only route through it, so
; there was never a reason to leave the route.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW — THE ROAD FORKS, AND THE LOOT IS BETWEEN THE BRANCHES:
;   (0, 25)          the stem, in from the Crossway. Both seam points are FIXED and unchanged:
;                    crossway_post's road leaves at world (0, -92) and the arena's gate path begins
;                    at world (0, -142), which are this cell's (0, 25) and (0, -25).
;   (0, 16)          THE FORK. Two rock-path markers, one either side.
;   west branch      (0,16) -> (-11,4) -> (-12,-10) -> (0,-25). The wider, more travelled one, past
;                    the Hollow Bowl and under Cairn Rise.
;   east branch      (0,16) -> (11,6) -> (13,-6) -> (0,-25). Narrower, through the Deadfall.
;   x -6..6, z -10..4    THE RUIN, between the branches and on neither of them: the standing wall,
;                    two pillars, a fallen one, the crate and all four pickups. You have to turn off
;                    the road to find any of it, and either branch will show it to you from outside.
;   x -22..-12, z 2..14  THE HOLLOW BOWL — encounter ground with a rock rim on three sides. A warband
;                    spawning here has cover and so does the player; a warband on the old straight
;                    path had neither.
;   x 12..24, z -18..-4  THE DEADFALL — a pine thicket the east branch runs through. Ambush ground.
;   (-19, -20)       CAIRN RISE, a 3.4x rock stack and the one landmark visible from anywhere in the
;                    cell. It is how you know which half of the fork you are on.
;
; ⚠️ EVERY STATIC PROP PARENTS TO Nav; ground cover and the rock-path markers do not, and carry no
; collider (see the ground-cover block below, which explains why at length and still applies).

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. ⚠️ AND THE agent_* DIMS DID NOT FOLLOW. On the 0.25 grid 1.75 and
; 0.5 were whole voxels; on this one they are not, so every bake quantised them and warned. The
; values below are the QUANTISED ones, so the file now says what the bake does: agent_height and
; agent_radius CEIL to a voxel (cell_height / cell_size), agent_max_climb FLOORS to cell_height.
; ⚠️ They encode this grid — change cell_size or cell_height and recompute all three with it.
[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_wn"]
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.5
cell_height = 0.4
agent_height = 2.0
agent_radius = 0.5
agent_max_climb = 0.4
agent_max_slope = 42.0

